1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,097
Tides is the big picture: the money flows behind every chart.

2
00:00:04,147 --> 00:00:07,711
Rates, the dollar, fear, credit, and where money is rotating.

3
00:00:08,164 --> 00:00:10,363
Open Tides on the dashboard.

4
00:00:10,413 --> 00:00:13,827
At the top, the Tide: coming in, slack, or going out.

5
00:00:13,877 --> 00:00:16,588
And the sea state: how rough the markets are.

6
00:00:17,071 --> 00:00:19,462
The winds apply it to each market.

7
00:00:19,512 --> 00:00:23,225
A tailwind helps longs there. A headwind works against them.

8
00:00:23,705 --> 00:00:28,698
Under it, the Navigator's daily note: today's readings in plain words, facts only.

9
00:00:29,149 --> 00:00:33,950
Storm warnings flag the big scheduled releases: the Fed, inflation, and jobs.

10
00:00:34,396 --> 00:00:38,643
The waves draw each current over time, with past event days marked.

11
00:00:39,106 --> 00:00:41,961
And each current, scored against its own last five years,

12
00:00:41,981 --> 00:00:43,694
with which way it's pulling.

13
00:00:44,148 --> 00:00:48,971
Today's AI Passage Plan applies all of this to your own assets and funnels.

14
00:00:49,021 --> 00:00:51,369
One plan a day, kept in your logbook.

15
00:00:51,832 --> 00:00:55,823
And you can add your own take: agree, disagree, and a short comment.
